  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Production Support Through Integrated FSL, WASH, and NFIs Responses to the Conflict Affected IDPs and Host Communities in Ar Rahad and  Sheikan Localities of North Kordufan State.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThis project will be implemented in A consortium with Alsalam Organization for Rural Development (AORD) and respond to the needs of the FSL, NFIs, and WASH sectors and directly align with SHF priorities focusing on life-saving assistance for the IDPs and vulnerable host communities in Sheikan and Ar Rahad localities in North Kordofan state. ltbrgtIn North Kordufan, currently, LMI and AORD are jointly implementing a WASH response project funded by SHF, aimed at increasing the resilience of crisis-affected IDPs, refugees, and host communities.ltbrgtBased on the needs identified through LM, AORD, the state-level cluster coordination, feedback from technical line ministries such as FAO,WES, MoH, and MoSW, and consultations with targeted locations, the project will respond with provision of cereals and vegetable seeds, agricultural tools, farmers and goats restocking, rehabilitation of HP and MWY, water chlorination, WMCs training, hygiene promoters training, hygiene awareness, emergency latrines constructions, provision of hand washing facilities and distribution of NFIs. ltbrgtthe activities are planned for 12 months to reach 55,781 affected population (14,317 women 16,107 girls 11,952 men 13,405 boys) including 1625 PWDs. The activities are designed based on the conflict sensitivity measures to avoid doing harm to the targeted communities and maximize the impact of the proposed interventions, the planned activities were proposed based on community consultation and technical line ministries and selected the best fit lifesaving interventions in the targeted communities.ltbrgtLM International&apos;s consortium will collaborate closely with SCI consortium in Ar Rahad and Sheikan localities, to enhance the effectiveness of their joint humanitarian efforts in FSL, WASH, and NFIs beside Health, Nutrition and shelter responses. Regular coordination meetings and joint needs assessments will be conducted to facilitate the sharing of data and strategies, ensuring that both organizations align their objectives and avoid duplication of efforts. By leveraging each consortium&#x2019;s strengths, LM International&#x2019;s consortium focuses on FSL, WASH and NFIs and SCI&#x2019;s consortium expertise in Health, Nutrition and Shelter, complementarities will be achieved allowing for integrated interventions that will address the diverse needs of affected populations. Resource optimization through shared logistics and community engagement process will further enhances the impact.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
